    fix(lane_target): repo-url rejects a home-rooted repo (CF-097)
    
    `repo-url` and `verify` probe the same kind of root but disagreed about what a
    valid root is: `verify_local` applies the `not_home_repo` check and rejects a
    path whose git top level IS $HOME (exit 4), while `check_repo_url` only compared
    the top level with the target and accepted that same path (exit 0).
    
    Measured at the pre-fix tip with HOME set to an initialized git repo:
      verify   <HOME> -> rc 4, `"check": "not_home_repo"`, `"ok": false`
      repo-url <HOME> -> rc 0, `PASS repo_url '<HOME>' -- root '<HOME>' HEAD <sha>`
    After the change both arms exit 4 for that path, and repo-url names the condition:
    `FAIL repo_url '<HOME>' -- not_home_repo: git top level is the home directory
    '<HOME>'`.
    
    `check_repo_url` now resolves the home exactly as `verify_local` resolves its
    default (`os.path.realpath(os.path.expanduser("~"))`) and raises RuntimeError,
    which `repo_urls()` already maps to exit 4, so no new exit code is introduced.
    The verify/workdir arm, the scan path and remote repo_urls are untouched: an
    ordinary non-home git root still PASSes exactly as before.
    
    Tests: a new `RepoURLHomeRoot` class drives both arms with HOME pointed inside
    the fixture -- the home-rooted repo is rejected by repo-url as well as by verify
    naming `not_home_repo`, a non-home real git root is still accepted, and a
    subdirectory of the home repo is still reported as the ordinary top-level
    mismatch rather than the home condition. The class is red against the pre-fix
    file (one failure at the repo-url exit-code assertion), so it pins the defect
    rather than restating the fix.
    
    tests/selftest.sh section 19 gains the matching arm plus a red control that runs
    the pre-fix revision from history: against a32f234 the arm prints
    `FAIL  repo-url accepted a home-rooted repo -- missing not_home_repo check
    (verify exit 4, repo-url exit 0)`, and the control prints the pre-fix acceptance.
    
    Gates: python3 -B tests/test_lane_target.py (43 tests, OK); bash tests/selftest.sh
    (SELFTEST: PASS); bash scripts/boardctl validate (RESULT: OK (7 warning(s)));
    bash docs/audits/cf198-section-mapping.sh (arms_plan=61 arms_tree=61, RESULT: OK).
    
    Addresses CF-097
